From: =?UTF-8?q?Juan=20Manuel=20L=C3=B3pez=20Carrillo?=
 <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 12:20:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 106/143] pci: sunxi: drop redundant SII IRQ lookup outside
 ITS-mode guard
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

sunxi_pcie_plat_request_irq() called platform_get_irq_byname(pdev,
"sii") unconditionally and aborted probe with -EINVAL if it was
missing.  The SII IRQ is only consumed by the non-ITS path inside the
"if (!pp->has_its)" block right below, which fetches it again -- the
outer fetch was both redundant and harmful: a board wired in ITS mode
(the msi-map DT property is present, so pp->has_its is true) can
legitimately omit the "sii" interrupt, and the unconditional lookup
would have failed probe before ever reaching the has_its check.

Drop the outer fetch.  The inner one inside the !has_its branch already
handles the error.

Signed-off-by: Juan Manuel López Carrillo <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c b/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
index a99399fbf..e12393cfc 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
@@ -801,10 +801,6 @@ static int sunxi_pcie_plat_request_irq(struct sunxi_pcie *sunxi_pcie, struct pla
 	struct sunxi_pcie *pci = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
 	struct sunxi_pcie_port *pp = &pci->pp;
 
-	irq = platform_get_irq_byname(pdev, "sii");
-	if (irq < 0)
-		return -EINVAL;
-
     if (!pp->has_its) {
         irq = platform_get_irq_byname(pdev, "sii");
         if (irq < 0)
